  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 305 AM EDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nOver the weekend through early next week, a closed mid-level low \nwill slide from the Florida Peninsula into the eastern Gulf. Warm \nand moist air wrapping around the low from the Atlantic will pool \nacross the area, supporting scattered showers and storms each day. \nHigh temperatures will remain in the 90s, combining with dewpoints \nin the 70s to drive heat index values into the upper 90s to low 100s.\n\nConfidence in the forecast starts to drop off by the Tuesday-\nWednesday timeframe, as model guidance has a large spread in the \npotential synoptic setup. Some of the guidance keeps the cut off low \nover the eastern Gulf, while other guidance has the low get absorbed \nby troughing to the north and shifting out of the area with drier \nand cooler air moving in with a wedge. There has been a slight trend \ntowards the latter solution, but confidence remains low in the \nforecast for mid to late next week.",
